# GymBlog.API Client Patterns

## Resolving the Client

Always get `GymBlogApiClient` from the service locator — never instantiate it:

```dart
final api = getIt<GymBlogApiClient>();
```

## Guard: Check If Configured

The API is optional (`GYMBLOG_API_URL` may be absent in `.env`).  
Always check before calling, or let `_ensureConfigured()` throw `GymBlogApiException` with `statusCode == 0`.

```dart
if (!GymBlogApiClient.isConfigured) return; // no-op when URL is missing
```

## Calling the API

```dart
// List
final rows = await api.getList('/api/customers');

// Single resource
final data = await api.get('/api/customers/$id');

// Mutations (POST/PUT/DELETE also invalidate the in-memory cache)
await api.post('/api/customers', body);
await api.put('/api/customers/$id', body);
await api.delete('/api/customers/$id');
```

## Handling Errors

Catch `GymBlogApiException`, not `DioException` — the client wraps all Dio errors.

```dart
try {
  final data = await api.get('/api/customers/$id');
} on GymBlogApiException catch (e) {
  if (e.statusCode == 401) { /* session expired */ }
  if (e.statusCode == 409) { /* conflict — check e.responseBody */ }
  Sentry.captureException(e);
  rethrow;
}
```

## Cache Behaviour

| Operation | Cache effect |
|-----------|-------------|
| `GET` | Served from cache if fresh (TTL 5 min; customers list: 2 min) |
| `GET` with `skipCache: true` | Bypasses cache, refreshes the entry |
| `POST` / `PUT` / `DELETE` | Auto-invalidates in-memory cache |

Call `GymBlogApiClient.clearCache()` after logout or on manual user refresh.

## Write Path — Prefer Offline Store

For data that must survive connectivity loss (customer mutations, workout edits) always use `OfflineLocalStore` + `PendingOperations` outbox instead of calling the API directly. Reserve direct API calls for **read-only** or **best-effort** operations.
